  "rows": [
    {
      "id": "actual-functional-contract",
      "a_actual_declaration": "IEANTN.CMSFunctional.Eligible, mass, positiveLeak, denominator, inverseObjective and SourceCMSFunctional; exact identities/lines are in declarations. No standalone historical Blueprint label; canonical correspondence is CMSFunctionalInput.v1 gap_reduction and shared Vocabulary.",
      "b_actual_primary": "CMS1708.04122v2,p2,Eq1.3: C+(A)=sup over even continuous REAL L1 nonzero F of [F(0)-A integral outside[-1,1](Fhat)+]/norm1(F). Fourier convention is exp(-2*pi*i*x*t). p5,Eqs1.11-1.12: B=limsup [pi(x+sqrtx)-pi(x)]/(sqrtx/logx),1<=B<=36/11.",
      "c_mechanism_and_verdict": "ALIGNED. Eligible matches the actual class, adds finite positive-part leakage and a genuine complex Fourier pair. It does not demand a peak at0, nonnegative F, bandlimit, or change F0 to supF. Physical F/G meet all fields through accepted mathematical proofs."
    },
    {
      "id": "universal-source-reduction",
      "a_actual_declaration": "SourceCMSFunctional and SourceCMSPopulation universally quantify any Eligible F,G with positive denominator; neither includes the Gaussian, .834021, or an unproved numerical enclosure.",
      "b_actual_primary": "CMS Theorem3/Eq1.13 and Corollary4/Eq1.14,p5; C+(A) nonincreasing statedp3 and definition1.3,p2.",
      "c_mechanism_and_verdict": "ALIGNED DERIVED SOURCE CONTRACT. Let M=integral absF>0,J=positiveLeak>=0,A0=36/11,D_A=F0-AJ. B<=A0 yields D_B>=D_A0>0; source supremum C+(B)>=D_B/M>=D_A0/M>0, hence1/C+(B)<=M/D_A0. Multiplying by1+2alpha is valid foralpha>=0. This exact general analytic consequence remains the explicit B premise; the CMS supremum/explicit-formula proof is not newly formalized."
    },
    {
      "id": "zero-and-one-indexing",
      "a_actual_declaration": "paperPrime n=Nat.nth Prime(n-1),primeAt n=Nat.nth Prime n; paper_gap_shift and zero_based_of_paper; canonical normalized_gap.",
      "b_actual_primary": "CMS Corollary4/Eq1.14,p5 uses the conventional one-based pn sequence.",
      "c_mechanism_and_verdict": "ALIGNED. For every naturaln,paperNormalizedGap(n+1)=normalizedGapn. The proof uses only source indexn+1>=1 and preserves eventuality. The helper atn0 is an aligned harmless totalization, never an out-of-domain material finding."
    },
    {
      "id": "limsup-and-onset",
      "a_actual_declaration": "EventualGapBound(c) means forall positiveepsilon,eventuallynormalizedGap<=c+epsilon; gaussian_gap_eventually and challenge_normalized_gap.",
      "b_actual_primary": "CMS Corollary4/Eq1.14,p5: limsup normalizedgap<=1/C+(B).",
      "c_mechanism_and_verdict": "ALIGNED. Epsilon/onset semantics are faithful to a finite upper limit superior. There is no claimed alln bound at exactc, no computed numerical onset, and no transfer to all realx>=exp44 or4. The separate strict comparison chooses half the positive difference to the fixed2026 coefficient."
    },
    {
      "id": "population-infimum-and-margin",
      "a_actual_declaration": "GoodCoefficient(alpha,c) keepsc>0 and existsdelta>0 eventuallyalpha+delta<=normalizedPopulation; SourceCMSPopulation explicitly records nonemptygoodset and infimum upper bound; population_from_functional.",
      "b_actual_primary": "CMS Theorem3/Eq1.13,p5: inf{c>0:liminf[pi(x+c sqrtxlogx)-pi(x)]/sqrtx>alpha}<=(1+2alpha)/C+(B),alpha>=0.",
      "c_mechanism_and_verdict": "ALIGNED. Positive eventualdelta is equivalent to the written strictliminf claim. Nonemptiness prevents a fake finite bound from Lean sInf-empty. The formal proof chooses a genuinely goodd below eachc strictly above the upper bound, then uses actual counting monotonicity. It never asserts infimum attainment or drops positiveepsilon."
    },
    {
      "id": "half-open-real-counts",
      "a_actual_declaration": "piReal(x)=Nat.primeCounting(floorNatx); halfOpenCount(c,x)=piReal(x+c sqrtxlogx)-piRealx; normalizedPopulation_mono and eventual_count_of_good.",
      "b_actual_primary": "CMS Theorem3/Eq1.13,p5 counts primes in(x,x+c sqrtxlogx], excluding lower but INCLUDING upper endpoint.",
      "c_mechanism_and_verdict": "ALIGNED. Exact half-open endpoint convention is retained. Proof-bearing source consumers are eventualpositivex, and monotonicity explicitly restrictsx>=2. Natural subtraction and nonpositive-real totalizations are not used to manufacture a source-domain conclusion."
    },
    {
      "id": "actual-eligibility-and-numerical-leaves",
      "a_actual_declaration": "gaussian_eligible uses genuine fourier_actual_physical, real continuity/evenness/L1F/L1G and actual F0 lower bound; challenge_integral_fourier_witness supplies physicalF/G plus full mass,positive exteriorleak and F0 bounds.",
      "b_actual_primary": "CMS Eq1.3,p2 specifies the class and exact functional. The rational witness and integral enclosures are project-internal proved numerical inputs, with no external attribution or unverified computation substituted.",
      "c_mechanism_and_verdict": "ALIGNED AND CLOSED D LEAVES. Exact bounds M<=.74899,J<=.031152,F0>=.999999999 are actual whole-real/full-wing integrals. The proved Fourier identity makes G the real transform. No independently assumed peak bound, Fourier certificate hypothesis, or output premise remains in the actual witness."
    },
    {
      "id": "typed-node-consumption",
      "a_actual_declaration": "GaussianFourierWitness.v1.challenge_objective_witness consumes integral_fourier_witness; RHAsymptoticGaussian.v1.challenge_normalized_gap/challenge_population_curve consume CMSinput,RHinput,and objective_witness.",
      "b_actual_primary": "CMS Theorem3/Corollary4 supply only the generic analytic reductions. The exact numerical inequalities and canonical ANT transports are project proofs.",
      "c_mechanism_and_verdict": "ALIGNED ACTUAL VALUE PATH. Raw witness uses full norm,full leakage,F0 and actual Eligible. Objective derivation uses all3 numerical enclosures to prove denominator positivity and inverseobjective<=.834021. Final consumers destructure and use hNumeric; actual11-root12-edge audit confirms source/RH/numerical argument use, not merely matching theorem types."
    },
    {
      "id": "current-fixed-gap-comparator",
      "a_actual_declaration": "gaussian_gap_eventually_lt_printed_2026 and canonical gap_below_printed_2026 compare only the literal.834050619151 coefficient.",
      "b_actual_primary": "Blanquer Robles,v2,21Nov2026,Zenodo24429650,DOI10.5281/zenodo.24429650,Theorem1,p1; Table1,p5 gives the witness numerical constant. Source was independently reviewed and its unchanged5Table1 numerical rows rerun in Published2026Review.",
      "c_mechanism_and_verdict": "ALIGNED. .834021<.834050619151 is exact; epsilon halfdifference gives eventualstrictcomparison. It is not a best-known census, proof of optimality or an explicit-onset comparison."
    },
    {
      "id": "historical-population-comparator",
      "a_actual_declaration": "gaussian_curve_lt_old_CPJ and finalSOURCE_LEDGER compare displayed.834021(1+2alpha) with.8358(1+2alpha),alpha>=0.",
      "b_actual_primary": "Chirre-Pereira Junior-de Laat,arXiv2005.02393v3,Section1.3,PDFp2 unnumbered optimized-bound display: under ordinaryRH the infimum ofstrict-liminf goodcoefficients is<.8358(1+2alpha).",
      "c_mechanism_and_verdict": "ALIGNED. The displayed upper-bound curve is strictly smaller for every nonnegativealpha. The true unknown infimum and the stronger2026two affine population curves/retunings are not claimed globally dominated. Final ledger now links exact primary locators and renders both source formulas."
    }
